# Satelles — Cursor AI Rules
# Mosquito risk + soil health map for Kočani Valley, North Macedonia

## Project Context
Satelles is a freemium public-good map. Two layers: mosquito breeding risk (red scale)
and soil health (green scale). Target users: farmers, municipalities, NGOs in Macedonia.
Mobile-first. No login. No ads. No friction.

## Tech Stack
- MapLibre GL JS (open source map renderer)
- OpenStreetMap base tiles (free)
- Google Earth Engine raster overlays (risk tiles via GEE tile URL or COG)
- Vanilla JS or Vite + vanilla (no React — keeps bundle tiny for mobile)
- Cloudflare Pages (free hosting)
- PWA manifest (Add to Home Screen, no app store)

## Architecture Rules
1. One HTML file entry point: index.html
2. Map fills 100% of viewport — no header, no sidebar, no footer
3. All UI floats on top, semi-transparent dark panels (rgba(0,0,0,0.7))
4. Layer switcher: three pill buttons top-center [Mosquito | Soil | Both]
5. Bottom-left: collapsible color legend
6. Top-right: geolocate + share buttons (WhatsApp & Viber deep links)
7. Top-left: village name search (simple geocoder)
8. Bottom-right: "Updated [date]" trust stamp
9. Click/tap on map cell: popup with risk score + last updated date

## Layers
### Mosquito Risk Layer
- Source: Google Earth Engine export or tile endpoint
- Color ramp: 0=transparent → 1=yellow → 0.6=orange → 1=red
- Formula: risk = water_presence × temp_window × days_since_flood × proximity_to_settlement
- GEE datasets: COPERNICUS/S1_GRD (SAR water), MODIS/061/MOD11A1 (LST), ECMWF/ERA5_LAND/HOURLY

### Soil Health Layer
- Source: existing GEE processing (Sentinel-2 NDVI, NDMI, NDWI)
- Color ramp: 0=red → 0.5=yellow → 1=green

## Coding Standards
- Mobile-first CSS. Touch targets ≥ 44px
- No login, no cookies banner, no modals on load
- Default language: Macedonian (mk). Use data-i18n attributes for future i18n
- Keyboard shortcuts on desktop: L = cycle layers, +/- = zoom, arrows = pan
- Hover tooltips on desktop, tap popups on mobile
- Keep JS files small and modular: map.js, layers.js, ui.js, geocoder.js

## File Structure
```
satelles/
├── index.html          # Entry point
├── manifest.json       # PWA manifest
├── sw.js               # Service worker (offline cache)
├── src/
│   ├── map.js          # MapLibre init + base map
│   ├── layers.js       # GEE tile layer management
│   ├── ui.js           # Pill switcher, legend, popups
│   └── geocoder.js     # Village name search
├── public/
│   ├── icon-192.png    # PWA icon
│   └── icon-512.png    # PWA icon
└── styles/
    └── main.css        # All styles
```

## GEE Integration Pattern
GEE tiles are served as XYZ tile URLs from a GEE App or Cloud Run function:
```
https://earthengine.googleapis.com/v1/projects/{project}/maps/{mapId}/tiles/{z}/{x}/{y}
```
For MVP: use static exported GeoTIFF or pre-rendered tile set from GEE.
For production: deploy a small Cloud Run function that refreshes tiles weekly.

## DO NOT build
- Login / accounts / email gate
- Dashboard, profile, settings
- Notification popups on first visit
- Analytics overlays, chatbot widgets
- Language picker (browser handles it)
- "Rate us" / newsletter modals
- App store install banners
